diff -ruN aubit4glsrc/node/README.md aubit4gl-aubit4gl_code-r12987-aubit4glsrc-trunk/node/README.md
--- aubit4glsrc/node/README.md	1969-12-31 19:00:00.000000000 -0500
+++ aubit4gl-aubit4gl_code-r12987-aubit4glsrc-trunk/node/README.md	2025-10-23 05:34:28.000000000 -0400
@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@
+You'll need nodejs and npm installing - on ubuntu : 
+
+	apt install nodejs npm
+
+Your distro may be different...
+
+
+Then - you'll need to the packages used :
+
+	npm install express net userid xml-js compression xml-escape passwd-linux uuid ssh2 authenticate-pam socket.io
+
+
+The code is in aubit4glsrc/node - make sure you've got the latest code from SVN - this will be changing a lot as development continues.
+
+If you want - you can install "extjs" and "sencha cmd" - but if you want to use the pregenerated html/javascript - just edit the node/server.js : 
+
+	//app.use(express.static(__dirname + '/html'));
+	app.use(express.static(__dirname + '/Aubit4GLWeb'));
+	//app.use(express.static(__dirname + '/Aubit4GLWeb/build/testing/Aubit4GLWeb'));
+
+uncomment the "/html" one - and comment out the "/Aubit4GLWeb" one - so it looks like this : 
+
+	app.use(express.static(__dirname + '/html'));
+	//app.use(express.static(__dirname + '/Aubit4GLWeb'));
+	//app.use(express.static(__dirname + '/Aubit4GLWeb/build/testing/Aubit4GLWeb'));
+
+and this should use the pre-build html/javascript - nothing else required.
+
+
+
+Put any 4ae's/4ge's you want to run in "node/baseProgs" (you can alter this later - but for testing let's just stick with doing it this way, the idea is to limit what users can run to pre-authorised executables)
+
+In baseProgs there's a script "runProgram.sh" - edit that to make sure AUBITDIR, INFORMIXDIR and any other settings are correct.
+In particular - your 
+	export INFORMIXDIR=/home/informix
+	export INFORMIXSERVER=ol_informix1210
+
+are likely to be different to mine.
+
+
+You'll then need to edit the applications.json file to list all the 4aes you can run (if you use 4ge as an extension - you'll need to set this in runProgram.sh)
+
+For example - my applications.json looks like this : 
+	[
+	{"name": "c1"}
+	,
+	{"name": "carlos"}
+	,
+	{"name": "cassens1"}
+	,
+	{"name": "customer", "ssh": { "host": "192.168.2.104", "path": "/home/aubit4gl/aubit4glsrc/node/baseProgs/customer.4ae" }  }
+	,
+	{"name": "displayAt"}
+	,
+	{"name": "displayToSrec"}
+	,
+	{"name": "eval"}
+	,
+	{"name": "getKey"}
+	,
+	{"name": "hello2"}
+	,
+	{"name": "menuLine"}
+	,
+	{"name": "msgBox"}
+	,
+	{"name": "openWindow"}
+	,
+	{"name": "prompt"}
+	,
+	{"name": "testp1"}
+	,
+	{"name": "testp2"}
+	,
+	{"name": "testportal"}
+	,
+	{"name": "user"}
+	]
+	
+There is a "makefile" in that baseProgs that compiles up all the 4gls as standalone programs (ie 4glpc a.4gl -o a.4ae) - and adds them to the applications.json file if you want to start with that..
+Obviously - you'll need to ensure all your forms are compiled up too. Again - the makefile tries to do that for all forms in that directory if you want to use that.
+
+
+Then - we have a "setuid_runner" program which will run things in baseProgs as a specified user - if you're happy - just compile that up with a "make" in the "node" directory
+(You can also edit that if you want to add further restrictions - you can also make it so its not required at all its just there so "USER" returns the correct value etc).
+It will be used by the "server.js" to start the "runProgram.sh". Alternatively - you can configure the applications.js to start programs using ssh - but for now - its easier to use setuid_runner.
+(it should still run if you dont chmod u+s on the setuid_runner - just everything will run as the user whos running the server)
+
+
+You can then start the service using : 
+
+node server.js 
+
+
+That should have you mostly up and running.
+(You can get it running on https - by setting up a certificate - but http should be fine for testing.)
+
+It should look something like this : 
+
+$ node server.js
+Script /home/aubit4gl/svn/aubit4gl-aubit4gl_code/aubit4glsrc/trunk/node/baseProgs/runProgram.sh exists and is executable
+Setuid binary /home/aubit4gl/svn/aubit4gl-aubit4gl_code/aubit4glsrc/trunk/node/setuid_runner exists and is executable
+File /home/aubit4gl/svn/aubit4gl-aubit4gl_code/aubit4glsrc/trunk/node/baseProgs/applications.json exists and is readable
+HTTPS server configured with SSL certificates
+__dirname=/home/aubit4gl/svn/aubit4gl-aubit4gl_code/aubit4glsrc/trunk/node
+Callback server listening on port 1234
+Express HTTP server listening on port 8080
+Express HTTPS server listening on port 8443
+
+
+You can then fire up your web browser (only tested in chrome) to whatever your server is - on port 8080 - on mine for example  
+    http://192.168.2.104:8080/index.html
+or
+    https://192.168.2.104:8443/index.html
+
+
+This should give you a login window.
+
+The program combo should be filled with the list of programs from your applications.json file, enter your normal linux username and password (the server.js should use standard password checks)
+NOTE: Your password will be sent in plain text for logging in - over https - this isnt an issue - but is "suboptimal" for http..
+
+Click "Login" and your program should start..
+
+
+
+
+
